{
  "topic": "What shooting stars are and where the Geminids come from",
  "language": "en",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "What is a shooting star? ✨",
  "hook": "What is a shooting star really? Spoiler: it's not a star.",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_hook",
      "narration": "What is a shooting star really? Spoiler: it's not a star.",
      "on_screen_text": "What is a shooting star?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shooting"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_grain",
      "narration": "It's almost always a speck of dust, about the size of a grain of sand.",
      "on_screen_text": "A grain of sand",
      "highlight_words": [
        "sand"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "It enters the atmosphere at tens of kilometers per second, far faster than a bullet.",
      "on_screen_text": "Faster than a bullet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "bullet"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "About a hundred kilometers up, it hits the air so fast that it makes it glow.",
      "on_screen_text": "The air glows",
      "highlight_words": [
        "glows"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_hook",
      "narration": "And it burns up high above, so there's no danger at all.",
      "on_screen_text": "No danger",
      "highlight_words": [
        "danger"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_orbit",
      "narration": "Every December, Earth crosses the dust trail of an asteroid called Phaethon.",
      "on_screen_text": "Phaethon's trail",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Phaethon's"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_radiant",
      "narration": "That's why we see the Geminid shower: they all seem to come from the constellation Gemini.",
      "on_screen_text": "They come from Gemini",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Gemini"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_watch",
      "narration": "To see them, find a dark spot and let your eyes adjust for about twenty minutes.",
      "on_screen_text": "Find a dark sky",
      "highlight_words": [
        "dark"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_stars",
      "narration": "You don't need a telescope: just your eyes and a little patience.",
      "on_screen_text": "Just your eyes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "eyes"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
