      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A shooting star is almost always a speck of dust entering the atmosphere very fast and making the air glow about 100 km up. Every December Earth crosses the trail of asteroid Phaethon and we see the Geminid shower. Original 3D animation; not to scale.",
